cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this prototype, please cite the paper that inspired it."
title: "Rocq Proof Slicer"
abstract: >-
  A declaration-level proof slicing prototype for Rocq/Coq, inspired by
  type-directed program slicing. The prototype uses Rocq's .glob reference
  table to compute a dependency closure from a target theorem, supports a
  proof-skeleton mode that replaces auxiliary proofs with Admitted, and can
  minimize a slice further with coqc as an oracle.
authors:
  - name: "The Rocq Proof Slicer contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2025-11-02
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Rocq
  - Coq
  - proof slicing
  - theorem proving
  - LLM
